# Round s2gates: the PAI tree's CPU node dumps of the Solar-Open2-250B Q4_K_M split set (four shards, 151.8 GB), `just dump-ref-solar2`:
# four prompts (41, 40, 114 and 1,536 ids) from ONE load, the layer taps of the first, each layer output of the next two, the last
# logits row of all four, and 64 greedy tokens of the first three. The phases run one after the other: the wall is their sum.
# Predicted wall [derived], seconds:
#   load      151.8 GB from the page cache (the shards were warm) through the CPU backend, which repacks every Q4_K/Q6_K weight to
#             its 8x8 interleave in anonymous memory (the log's `repack tensor ... q4_K_8x8`): measured 185 s on the first run
#             (the first prediction, 0-60 s, took the loader for a map); a cold read adds ~50 s at ~3 GB/s
#   prefill   1,731 ids x 2 x 13.9 G MACs (the design's active count: KDA layers 4.96 B, GQA 1.31 B, shared 0.76 B, routers 0.06 B,
#             routed 6.04 B, head 0.81 B) = 48 TFLOP; the 1,536-id prompt is three 512-row ubatches that each read every expert once
#             (1.3 s at 120 GB/s). The one term derivation does not close: the 32-thread ggml CPU rate on Q4_K/Q6_K rows,
#             expected 1-2 TFLOP/s (0.5 pessimistic): 25-100 s
#   greedy    192 tokens at 8.7 GB read a token (5.1 non-routed + 3.66 routed) over ~120 GB/s host DRAM: 15 s
#   writes    ~0.6 GB of f32 node files: 5 s
#   total     measured 251 s (09:19:35Z-09:23:46Z): load 185 s, the four prompts and 192 greedy tokens 66 s; bound 1800 s.
# What the run guarantees: CUDA hidden, the CPU lease held, no peer on the box's cores (the lease), the staging set installed only
# when each prompt's manifest carries its `# complete` trailer.
kind: exclusive
reason: solar2_dump runs the PAI tree on 32 CPU threads and maps the whole 151.8 GB split set, evicting that much of the page cache
  (the V4.1 and GLM host sets among it); beside a timed run or a gate batch it would take their cores and their memory
  bandwidth, so it holds the lease; why now: the Solar-Open2 oracle every body round (s2step, s2prefill) is judged against
  (round s2gates)
minutes: 3..5
